Third-Party Components

This application bundles or integrates separate software. Their licenses apply
independently:

| Component | License | Source |
|-----------|---------|--------|
| rhwp (HWPX editor core) | See upstream | https://github.com/edwardkim/rhwp |
| WhiteBoard4Share (wb4s) | See upstream | https://github.com/soonpyopark/WhiteBoard4Share |
| FortuneSheet | MIT | https://github.com/ruilisi/fortune-sheet |
| TipTap | MIT | https://github.com/ueberdosis/tiptap |
| Yjs / y-websocket | MIT | https://github.com/yjs/yjs |
| Electron | MIT | https://github.com/electron/electron |
| React | MIT | https://github.com/facebook/react |
| Other npm packages | See package.json | https://www.npmjs.com/ |

Editor core versions are recorded in `lib/cores-manifest.json`. Offline USB
packages may be placed under `lib/updates/` (see `lib/updates/README.md`).

Rhwp studio WASM bundles (`public/rhwp-studio/`, `public/rhwp-core/`) and
wb4s editor bundles (`public/wb4s-editor/`) are built from upstream sources
during `npm run build` and are not authored in this repository.

Chromium (via Electron) and other native binaries included in portable builds
are subject to their respective licenses (e.g. `LICENSE.electron.txt`,
`LICENSES.chromium.html` in the Electron distribution output).
